# Stack: Horizontal and Vertical in a column, where Horizontal aligns the items and Vertical distributes the leftover height.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Stack · Alignment in a column
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: column
			Direction: vertical
			Gap: 4
			Box:
				Height: 120
				Border: 0.5
				Border color: rule
				Background: tint
		For style: narrow
			Direction: vertical
			Gap: 4
			Box:
				Border: 0.5
				Border color: rule
				Background: tint
	Section:
		Text: Stack
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Alignment in a column
		Paragraph: With `Direction: vertical` the roles swap. `Horizontal` aligns the items in the width (`stretch` by default) and `Vertical` distributes the leftover height, which needs a `Height` on the `Stack`.
			Style: intro
		Grid:
			Column sizes: repeat(4, *)
			Gap: 6 10
